[ti:Lyrics Test]
[ar:Test Artist]
[al:Test Album]
[au:Test Author]
[by:SPL Tester]

; SPL is LRC-compatible: a stamp opens the line and the body follows.
[00:00.00]This is the first line of the song.
[00:01.72]Here comes the second line more words.
[00:04.28]A third line to complete the verse.
[00:06.16]The chorus begins right about now
[00:07.82]Singing la la la la la la la
[00:09.54]This is the final line of the test song.
[00:12.36]Fading away slowly.
; A stamp may leave the fraction out: SPL reads the missing digits as the
; omitted low ones, so this is the same as [00:13.00].
[00:13]End of track.

; The features SPL adds on top of LRC, in the order the standard introduces them.
; Adjacent leading stamps share one text: this line starts at both stamps.
[00:14.00][00:16.00]A repeated line.
; A stamp inside the line starts the word after it, and the trailing one ends it.
[00:18.00]Word by[00:19.00]word[00:20.00]
; A non-start marker may use angle brackets, which is what lets the row arrive
; before its first word starts.
[00:21.00]<00:22.00>Late[00:23.00]arrival[00:24.00]
; Two lines with one stamp are a lyric line and its translation.
[00:25.00]A translated line.
[00:25.00]Une ligne traduite.
; A translation may leave its stamp out, and a stamp with no text after it ends
; the line above instead of writing a line of its own.
[00:27.00]Another translated line.
Sans horodatage.
[00:28.00]
